<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 39 µm in Botryllus schlosseri (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 82.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Periodic Schnakenberg kinetics on a 271.04 µm window (seven wavelengths). The onset formula is pinned to λ = 38.72 µm. The nonlinear activator FFT measured 39.90 µm (6.79 cycles). Pearson r between the formula and argmax σ(k) across a 10-point γ sweep is 0.999998 (RMSE 1.598 cells). Equal diffusion is stable (σ_peak = -0.649). The Parent 1991 colony photograph has circularity 0.085 against a circle reference of 1. The GIF is a spot field in the colony colour histogram, not a reconstruction of the star systems. Overall 82.5/100 (faithfulness 80.1, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 912735 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 5354b05f2dc4818de3ea1a571dfd69e0a0520f9e5224fbb62dc6410973b5e8f1 (sha256 5354b05f2dc4818de3ea1a571dfd69e0a0520f9e5224fbb62dc6410973b5e8f1), spec_fingerprint 1f41527fdb3ad32975a5fe85bdbd97d229f23905e445211f557d1ede5e6ef301. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1f41527fdb3ad32975a5fe85bdbd97d229f23905e445211f557d1ede5e6ef301; artifact_sha256: 5354b05f2dc4818de3ea1a571dfd69e0a0520f9e5224fbb62dc6410973b5e8f1; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0/Botryllus_schlosseri_Parent1991_Banyuls.jpg=e351975e1a0b4822...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber when two morphogens diffuse at different rates. | Schnakenberg 1979: the mass-action system f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Sorrentino, Manni, Lane and Burighel 2000: ascidian larvae carry a cerebral vesicle with sensory organs, including an ocellus. | Cloney 1982: review of ascidian larval metamorphosis, including colonial botryllids.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3136 parameters a=0.097, b=1.246, γ=1.37 chosen so the onset formula returns λ=3.872e-5 m on a 7-wavelength periodic window. | Nonlinear spectral integration, γ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, specimen segmentation, KS orientation test, and seed-ensemble CV.; transfer_boundary: Kondo and Asai 1995 established a reaction-diffusion wavelength for Pomacanthus pigment stripes. That measurement is not transferred as a Botryllus datum. | The 39 µm length is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment, not a published caliper on the Parent 1991 photograph.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that Botryllus star systems are produced by this PDE. | Does not claim the colony photograph was taken at 39 µm. | Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this audit.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Add a diffusivity-ratio sweep with D_u fixed and D_v/D_u varied above r_c, and record whether λ(r) is monotonic.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add an autocatalysis knockout (drop the u^2 v term) and show that the growth-rate peak is no longer positive.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Save the ratio-sweep RMSE next to the existing Pearson r, KS statistic, and spacing CV in the metrics JSON.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.25e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

