<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 39 µm in Botryllus schlosseri (Holocene, detail scale) (Botryllus schlosseri)",
        "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 39 µm in Botryllus schlosseri (Holocene, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Botryllus schlosseri morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Botryllus schlosseri specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Botryllus schlosseri" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this audit.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim that Botryllus star systems are produced by this PDE.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the colony photograph was taken at 39 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nonlinear spectral integration, γ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, specimen segmentation, KS orientation test, and seed-ensemble CV.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3136 parameters a=0.097, b=1.246, γ=1.37 chosen so the onset formula returns λ=3.872e-5 m on a 7-wavelength periodic window.",
        "reported_in_source: Cloney 1982: review of ascidian larval metamorphosis, including colonial botryllids.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the mass-action system f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Sorrentino, Manni, Lane and Burighel 2000: ascidian larvae carry a cerebral vesicle with sensory organs, including an ocellus.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber when two morphogens diffuse at different rates.",
        "transfer_boundary: Kondo and Asai 1995 established a reaction-diffusion wavelength for Pomacanthus pigment stripes. That measurement is not transferred as a Botryllus datum.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 39 µm length is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment, not a published caliper on the Parent 1991 photograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Botryllus schlosseri" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Botryllus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; output: docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Botryllus schlosseri; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber when two morphogens diffuse at different rates. | Schnakenberg 1979: the mass-action system f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Sorrentino, Manni, Lane and Burighel 2000: ascidian larvae carry a cerebral vesicle with sensory organs, including an ocellus. | Cloney 1982: review of ascidian larval metamorphosis, including colonial botryllids.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3136 parameters a=0.097, b=1.246, γ=1.37 chosen so the onset formula returns λ=3.872e-5 m on a 7-wavelength periodic window. | Nonlinear spectral integration, γ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, specimen segmentation, KS orientation test, and seed-ensemble CV.; transfer_boundary: Kondo and Asai 1995 established a reaction-diffusion wavelength for Pomacanthus pigment stripes. That measurement is not transferred as a Botryllus datum. | The 39 µm length is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment, not a published caliper on the Parent 1991 photograph.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that Botryllus star systems are produced by this PDE. | Does not claim the colony photograph was taken at 39 µm. | Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this audit.]; phenomenon_size: 39 µm (3.872e-05 m, log10=-4.412 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 39 µm to 6.2 cm): 39 µm:botryllus-schlosseri-bioelectric-polarity, 72 µm:botryllus-schlosseri-vertex-packing, 1.4 mm:botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength, 2.5 mm:botryllus-schlosseri-clock-wavefront, 8.2 mm:botryllus-schlosseri-morphogen-condensation, 1.1 cm:botryllus-schlosseri-flux-canalization, 1.1 cm:botryllus-schlosseri-elastic-buckling, 1.4 cm:botryllus-schlosseri-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1046/j.1463-6395.2000.00054.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/icb/22.4.817>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
